---
import Lamp from "@/layouts/Lamp.astro";
import { CONTACT } from "@/lib/site";
---

<Lamp title="Privacy" description="Morse Lamp keeps your progress on your device and collects nothing.">
  <main class="prose-lamp flex-1 pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm text-fg-dim hover:text-fg">Morse Lamp</a>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-fg-dim">18 October 2026</p>

    <h2>What the app stores</h2>
    <p>
      Morse Lamp keeps your progress and settings on your device only: which characters you have
      unlocked, how accurately you have keyed and recognised them, your measured dit length, and
      the switches in Settings. Nothing leaves the phone.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. Morse Lamp does not collect, transmit or share any data. It has no accounts, no
      analytics, no advertising and no network access of any kind. It never connects to the
      internet.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Deleting the app deletes everything it stored. Settings → Reset progress wipes your progress
      while keeping the app installed.
    </p>

    <h2>Apple</h2>
    <p>
      If you install Morse Lamp through TestFlight or the App Store, Apple collects its own data,
      such as crash logs and download counts, under Apple's privacy policy. None of it reaches me
      with anything that identifies you.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
  <footer class="mt-16 py-8 text-sm text-fg-dim">
    <nav aria-label="Footer" class="flex gap-6"><a href="/" class="hover:text-fg">Home</a><a href="/support" class="hover:text-fg">Support</a></nav>
  </footer>
</Lamp>
